id Gradle plugin written, or seen in a tool result), 'android_command' (adb, the emulator, sdkmanager, avdmanager, react-native run-android or a Gradle variant task). The edit values 'swift_edit', 'kotlin_edit' and 'java_edit' are reserved for rules that need no other evidence; no rule sends them yet. 'project_scan', for any kind: a scan of the session's git repository. The CLI scans when the process starts and sends the result. After each conversation_reset, it sends the latest scan's result again. A conversation whose scan did not find every kind scans again, uncached, when its first message arrives, so a kind that scan missed can come after that message. A client that needs to tell project evidence from conversation evidence checks for 'project_scan'. More values will be added; ignore one you do not recognize. Absent from CLI versions that predate the field, which send only conversation evidence."),uuid:p(),session_id:o()}).describe("@internal The conversation, or the git repository it runs in, shows a known kind of development work, for hosts that key tooling on it (Claude Code Desktop opens its iOS Simulator entry point on ios_app). Sent with trigger as its only other payload. Per conversation per process, each kind is sent at most once from conversation evidence and at most once from the project scan. Conversation evidence is sent when it first completes, or at startup when a resumed conversation already has it. Project evidence comes from a CLI process in print mode (-p), which is how the Agent SDK and Claude Code Desktop start it. It is sent at startup, after each conversation_reset, and at the first message of a conversation whose earlier scan did not find every kind. Either can arrive before system/init. A rewind or compaction never retracts it and only a conversation_reset starts over. Treat each kind as a sticky fact about the conversation: a client that needs only the kind can ignore repeats, and one that needs to know what set it off reads trigger.")),